notes:
The page links one other kill chain, and four defense topics.

A week after this incident, the Shai-Hulud worm went after the same target, maintainers' npm publishing rights, and it has its own kill chain. Read the two together to see what changed when the republication step was automated.

The page's related defense topics are CI/CD security, non-human identity, Git and version control, and detection engineering. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
